{"availability":"available","full":"hou-yz/MultiviewX","name":"MultiviewX","description":"Toolkits for the synthetic multiview pedestrian detection dataset, MultiviewX.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":43,"forks":7,"created":"2020-02-16T10:57:21Z","updated":"2024-05-11T10:41:04Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://hou-yz.github.io/publication/2020-eccv2020-mvdet","topics":["dataset","detection","multiview","pedestrian-detection"],"demo":"https://hou-yz.github.io/publication/2020-eccv2020-mvdet","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:24.744Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:24.744Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:24.744Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T20:15:24.744Z","stars":43,"forks":7}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The MultiviewX dataset is dedicated to multiview synthetic pedestrian detection. Using pedestrian models from PersonX, in Unity, we build a novel synthetic dataset MultiviewX. It follows the WILDTRACK dataset for set-up, annotation, and structure.","The MultiviewX dataset is generated on a 25 meter by 16 meter playground. It has 6 cameras that have overlapping field-of-view. The images in MultiviewX dataset are of high resolution, 1920x1080, and are synchronized. To fully exploit the complementary views, calibrations are also provided in MultiviewX dataset."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hou-yz/MultiviewX/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"24b6169079b25219787c74f28d4236e8c09246e6eafb2c38ff3c4619af4f9482","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:24.862Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:24.862Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The MultiviewX dataset is dedicated to multiview synthetic pedestrian detection. Using pedestrian models from PersonX, in Unity, we build a novel synthetic dataset MultiviewX. It follows the WILDTRACK dataset for set-up, annotation, and structure.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ho